{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fragrant-tainted-lice","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe runner attaches per-call usage to every result (`result[\"_usage\"]`, src/rebar/llm/runner.py:543) but Pass-1 drops it: passes.py:331 reads only findings, and BatchRunResult.outputs (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:167-176) carries no usage key — so plan-review coverage.metrics has call counts but zero token totals for the most expensive pass (the gap is documented at src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:139-149). Per-criterion request/tool-call counts are extracted (runner.py:_extract_usage) but never persisted, blocking data-driven criterion demotion decisions.\n\n## Approach\nAccumulate `_usage` across every runner.run call inside run_pass1 (single-turn chunks, AGENT criteria, container pairings, prerequisite calls): an aggregate sum plus a per-criterion map {llm_calls, requests, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens}. Emit the aggregate in BatchRunResult.outputs[\"_usage\"] so _attach_plan_review_metrics (src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:249+) folds real token totals into coverage.metrics, and persist the per-criterion map into the REVIEW_RESULT sidecar coverage (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py). Alternative rejected: post-hoc parsing of the REBAR_USAGE_LOG JSONL — opt-in, not always present, and not keyed by criterion.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py, src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py, tests/llm/test_pass1_usage.py.\n\n## Testing\nUnit with FakeRunner emitting stub _usage dicts: aggregate totals equal the sum over calls; per-criterion map keys match the routed criteria; sidecar payload carries the map; a runner result without _usage degrades to zeros without error.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] After a review, coverage.metrics contains input/output/cache token totals that include Pass-1 calls (checked: unit test summing FakeRunner stub usage).\n- [ ] The sidecar coverage carries a per-criterion usage map for every routed criterion (checked: sidecar payload unit test).\n- [ ] Missing _usage on any call degrades gracefully to zero contribution (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] Code-review finalize's existing token metrics are unchanged (checked: existing finalize tests pass).","id":"d52a-40cd-75d4-46cb","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Thread Pass-1 per-call usage and per-criterion request counts into batch outputs and the sidecar"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785384355519377001,"uuid":"3ce86459-bfb5-40f2-94f8-eac5a82f1b12"}